+## Deploy 1: Code Removal & Zero-Downtime Preparation (Shipped)
 
-### Safety Guarantees Verified
-- **Safe alongside Release 0:** Zero database migrations, zero changes to `db/schema.rb`, and zero modifications to `consul_development` data. Release 0 can continue serving normally while Deploy 1 rolls out.
-- **Safe alongside Deploy 2:** All columns scheduled to be dropped in Deploy 2 are listed in `self.ignored_columns` on their surviving models so already-booted Deploy 1 processes will not raise `PG::UndefinedColumn` when Deploy 2 runs its migrations. Verified with a live simulation dropping all target tables and columns without resetting ActiveRecord column caches.
-- **Safe against existing proposal data in PostgreSQL:** Transitional guards prevent `NameError: uninitialized constant Proposal / ProposalNotification` and `NoMethodError` / `ArgumentError` on all surviving pages (homepage, polls, user profiles, account, notifications, moderation, admin, management, GraphQL, communities/topics, comments) while legacy rows remain in `consul_development` between Deploy 1 and Deploy 2.
